        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            A pickleball paddle can cost anywhere from about $20 to over $250, but most players are best served between $60 and $150. That range already includes carbon faces, honeycomb cores and dependable builds, and it costs about the same per hour of play as a cheap paddle while playing better for its whole life.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Start cheap only if you are still deciding whether you like the game, step up to the mid-range once you play weekly, and save premium and flagship paddles for when you can genuinely feel what they add. Whatever you spend, a few lessons will do more for your game than the last $100 of paddle.
          </p>
